1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,500
<i> Earlier, that black car,</i>

2
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:02,500
<i> I thought it was following me.</i>

3
00:00:02,633 --> 00:00:03,933
<i>I really feel like
I have a stalker.</i>

4
00:00:04,067 --> 00:00:05,667
<i>Buddy, stop it!
That's enough!</i>

5
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:06,967
<i> Major Delgado!</i>

6
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,400
<i>You're not in a position
to fight back, Major Delgado.</i>

7
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:11,700
<i>Don't add more offenses
to your record.</i>

8
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:13,600
<i>You might never return
to the service.</i>

9
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:14,800
<i> On the day Ramon left,</i>

10
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:16,400
<i> he left something with me.</i>

11
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:17,400
<i> He told me to give this...</i>

12
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:19,033
<i>if anything bad happened to him.</i>

13
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:20,333
<i> Jay's Pro Gym.</i>

14
00:00:20,467 --> 00:00:22,833
<i>Do you know
where his locker is here?</i>

15
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:26,200
<i>Why do you even need
to install CCTV?</i>

16
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,633
<i>We need to make sure Joey
doesn't have a stalker.</i>

17
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:31,267
<i> Metropolitan State University.</i>

18
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,500
<i> Buddy, I know you.</i>

19
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:34,700
<i>I know you still have
a lot you want to say to me.</i>

20
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:36,767
<i> On the night Ramon died...</i>

21
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,467
<i> I was with Golda.</i>

22
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,900
<i> So it was true after all.</i>

23
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:41,833
<i> She's my informant.</i>

24
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,567
<i> I already told your sibling.</i>

25
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,333
<i>I don't want strangers
coming here.</i>

26
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:48,900
<i>What if someone tries
to kill me again?</i>

27
00:00:49,033 --> 00:00:50,033
<i>The video you recorded is here.</i>

28
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:51,500
<i>It was wrong for us
to delete that video.</i>

29
00:00:51,633 --> 00:00:53,033
<i> I'm under investigation...</i>

30
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:55,500
<i>for the death of
Staff Sergeant Ramon Orbos.</i>

31
00:00:55,633 --> 00:00:57,100
<i>- What?
- I had nothing to do with that.</i>

32
00:00:57,233 --> 00:00:58,567
<i>I know you're not
the one who did it.</i>

33
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,533
<i> Let's meet right now.</i>

34
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:21,700
I was hoping
that you could help me...

35
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:26,267
by giving me trusted contacts
in the police force,

36
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:29,533
if it's okay to talk to them.

37
00:01:32,733 --> 00:01:34,567
Andrew...

38
00:01:35,533 --> 00:01:37,733
When I was starting,

39
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:43,233
I built my own contacts.

40
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,867
I didn't expect help
from anyone else.

41
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:47,767
I...

42
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:51,200
I built my sources,

43
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,667
my name.

44
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:55,900
And...

45
00:01:56,567 --> 00:01:58,733
all that hard work,

46
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,200
you benefited from it.

47
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:04,600
I know, Mom.

48
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,700
That's why I'm doing my best,

49
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:10,633
so I can follow in
your footsteps.

50
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:35,900
Andrew!

51
00:02:36,033 --> 00:02:37,100
You're here.

52
00:02:37,967 --> 00:02:40,533
I thought the kids here
were just joking.

53
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:44,033
Mom is already sleeping.

54
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:45,633
Don't worry.
She's asleep.

55
00:02:45,767 --> 00:02:47,567
She's on her meds.

56
00:02:47,733 --> 00:02:51,567
Come, I have a small gathering
outside with some sponsors.

57
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:55,400
And they're asking where
my famous sibling is.

58
00:02:55,533 --> 00:02:57,600
So come on.

59
00:02:57,733 --> 00:02:59,033
Maybe you can convince them

60
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:01,867
to open their checkbooks again.

61
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,867
Okay? Let's go.

62
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,267
She's going to be okay.

63
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:11,167
Let's go, come on.

64
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,067
Hon!

65
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,433
Look who I found.

66
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,267
- Oh, Andrew.
- Boss Idol.

67
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,633
So nice to see you.

68
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:29,467
Well, I just came to visit mom.

69
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,200
I wanted to ask her
about business, about work.

70
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:33,767
Work?

71
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:36,500
Oh, do you need help, Andrew?

72
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:42,800
You know you can always rely
on me to help you, right?

73
00:03:43,833 --> 00:03:46,000
Remember your exposé on Delgado?

74
00:03:51,967 --> 00:03:53,100
Before you talk about that...

75
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,133
Okay, later, all right?

76
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,133
The guests are looking at you.

77
00:03:57,267 --> 00:03:59,667
Of course, they want
to meet Boss Idol.

78
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,300
Come on, do that later.

79
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:03,067
Of course.

80
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,667
Don't worry, Brother.

81
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,467
If I ever need your help,
you're the one I'll go to.

82
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,333
Okay.

83
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:11,400
For now, let's focus on
the party,

84
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:13,800
so my sister doesn't get upset.

85
00:04:13,933 --> 00:04:15,367
All right, all right.

86
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,933
- Okay.
- Go ahead.

87
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:19,467
Come on.
Hi, hi, mates.

88
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,133
- Hello.
- Meet Boss Idol.

89
00:04:22,267 --> 00:04:24,033
Good afternoon, hi.

90
00:04:24,167 --> 00:04:25,200
Nice to meet you.

91
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:27,600
Nice to meet you,
nice to meet you.

92
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,233
- Oh, are you going home?
- Ah, not yet.

93
00:04:35,367 --> 00:04:37,500
I'm waiting for dad.
He said he'd pick me up.

94
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:38,933
I'll stay here for now.

95
00:04:40,133 --> 00:04:41,633
You're really hard to talk to!

96
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:44,300
Sir, an ID is really required
before entering, Sir.

97
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:46,067
Or you can just call them

98
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,333
and talk outside.

99
00:04:58,333 --> 00:05:01,900
<i>Ah, we needed to recover
a recorded video,</i>

100
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:03,667
<i>but they said someone
from your side already came</i>

101
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,367
<i>to update it, so it was deleted.</i>

102
00:05:11,967 --> 00:05:14,467
Oh, I thought your dad
was picking you up?

103
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:18,200
There! The one in red!

104
00:05:18,333 --> 00:05:19,633
- Hey!
- Hey!

105
00:05:22,567 --> 00:05:23,667
You know what?

106
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:27,633
You have the potential
to be a serious broadcaster

107
00:05:27,767 --> 00:05:29,367
just like your mom.

108
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:32,100
I remember back in her days,

109
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:35,867
she used to cover
international issues.

110
00:05:38,367 --> 00:05:42,333
You don't really need
to go to another country

111
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:46,000
to be a serious journalist.

112
00:05:46,133 --> 00:05:48,233
What I'm doing is important too.

113
00:05:48,367 --> 00:05:50,400
Sister, it looks like Kisses
and the others

114
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:52,200
are getting bored over there.

115
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:53,533
I'll go keep them company.

116
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:55,700
Okay.

117
00:05:55,833 --> 00:05:56,800
Excuse me.

118
00:05:56,933 --> 00:05:58,567
Thank you.

119
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:19,100
Hey! Hey!

120
00:06:21,767 --> 00:06:23,333
- Ouch! What the heck?
- Sorry, I'm sorry!

121
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:24,500
You didn't watch
where you were going!

122
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:25,567
- Ouch! What the heck?
- Sorry, I'm sorry!

123
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:28,567
You jerk!
Come back here!

124
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,967
Move aside!

125
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,600
- Ouch!
- Move! Move! Move!

126
00:06:35,733 --> 00:06:37,067
Move!

127
00:06:40,333 --> 00:06:42,867
Hey! Let's go! Hurry!

128
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:46,200
You too, finish your food.

129
00:06:46,333 --> 00:06:47,767
Go on, go on.

130
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:48,900
- Uncle Andrew!
- Yes.

131
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:51,200
Uncle Andrew.

132
00:06:51,333 --> 00:06:52,467
- Uncle Andrew.
- What are you guys doing here?

133
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,033
- How's the food?
- Actually, we're bored.

134
00:06:54,167 --> 00:06:55,767
Can I play video games,
Uncle Andrew.

135
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,633
Videogames?
Of course, let's do it.

136
00:06:57,767 --> 00:07:01,933
Yay! Uncle Andrew,
I missed playing with you.

137
00:07:04,867 --> 00:07:06,600
- Did you miss me?
- Yes.

138
00:07:16,867 --> 00:07:17,933
Get changed, okay?

139
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:20,233
And then we're gonna play later,
okay?

140
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:21,700
I just need to go somewhere.

141
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:22,867
- Okay, Sir.
- Let's go, Kisses.

142
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:23,933
Let's get changed.

143
00:07:24,067 --> 00:07:25,200
Miss, you handle things here,
okay?

144
00:07:25,333 --> 00:07:27,133
Yes, Sir.

145
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,800
Lord, please,
I hope they pass by already.

146
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:30,833
<i> What if someone sneaks in?</i>

147
00:08:30,967 --> 00:08:34,100
<i>What if someone gets inside
the house? What then?</i>

148
00:08:34,233 --> 00:08:37,933
<i>What if someone tries
to kill me again, Andrew?</i>

149
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,567
Plastic! Plasti...

150
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:01,933
Hey, kid, did you see
a woman wearing a red jacket?

151
00:09:02,067 --> 00:09:03,833
My sibling ran away from me.

152
00:09:10,367 --> 00:09:12,667
<i>Your number cannot be
completed nor dialed.</i>

153
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,833
<i>Check the number and dial again.</i>

154
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,133
I think I got hurt!

155
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,767
I might've sprained something.

156
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,233
Oh, guard, mister...

157
00:09:24,367 --> 00:09:26,867
Do you know my child,
Joey Delgado?

158
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,567
Fair-skinned girl,
about this tall,

159
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:31,067
hair like this.

160
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,767
Yes, Sir, she was here.

161
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,100
She said...

162
00:09:34,233 --> 00:09:35,367
she'd wait for you here,

163
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,800
but she suddenly left.

164
00:09:36,933 --> 00:09:38,900
She went that way,
to the market.

165
00:09:40,167 --> 00:09:41,767
- The market?
- Yes.

166
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:46,233
Oh no, those men who shoved me
were there too.

167
00:09:46,367 --> 00:09:49,667
It looked like they were chasing
a woman as well.

168
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:52,067
Thank you.

169
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:55,600
Oh, wearing red?

170
00:09:55,733 --> 00:09:58,233
She went that way, that way.

171
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,167
Thank you.

172
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,500
I thought you were going
to turn me in.

173
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:10,767
Hindi, ah.

174
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:13,367
I'm letting you go, pretty lady.

175
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,167
Prank lang!

176
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:16,767
Just a prank!

177
00:10:20,967 --> 00:10:22,000
Here.

178
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:26,067
Oh.

179
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:28,900
This is for you.
My mom cooked it.

180
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:30,100
It's good.

181
00:10:30,233 --> 00:10:32,067
Thank you!

182
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,200
Thank you.

183
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:34,933
Bye!

184
00:10:52,167 --> 00:10:54,267
Looks like that kid fooled us.

185
00:10:55,167 --> 00:10:56,867
Seems like the woman
already got away.

186
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,133
Are you already giving up?

187
00:10:58,267 --> 00:11:00,167
You want Madam to chew us out?

188
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:01,267
Let's split up.

189
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,233
You go back there.
I'll stay here.

190
00:11:17,733 --> 00:11:18,667
Who are you?

191
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:21,233
Wait.

192
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,600
I know Mr. Limjoco.

193
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:26,300
You know him? Then why didn't
you go straight to the party?

194
00:11:29,633 --> 00:11:30,733
Tell me the truth.

195
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,167
Who are you and
what are you doing here?

196
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,667
Relax.

197
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:38,767
I'll explain.

198
00:12:07,933 --> 00:12:10,200
<i> Mom!</i>

199
00:12:11,467 --> 00:12:13,700
<i>- Son...
- Mom...</i>

200
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,200
That's enough.

201
00:12:23,333 --> 00:12:25,067
Were you with the one
who shot my mother?

202
00:12:26,867 --> 00:12:28,700
Did you come here
to finish the job?

203
00:12:31,433 --> 00:12:32,467
What?

204
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,133
You won't stop, huh?

205
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,333
This is so good!

206
00:12:41,467 --> 00:12:43,333
The person who gave this
to you is really nice.

207
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,967
I'm nicer!

208
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:47,167
I even helped her escape...

209
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,600
from those ugly men.

210
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:52,300
So you're the hero now!

211
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,567
Kid...

212
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:59,067
You said you helped someone.

213
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,967
Was it a woman or a man?

214
00:13:06,867 --> 00:13:08,667
Don't be scared.
I'm a police officer.

215
00:13:17,367 --> 00:13:18,667
Oh, there.

216
00:13:26,633 --> 00:13:27,800
It was a woman
that I have helped.

217
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,433
Where did she go?

218
00:13:49,833 --> 00:13:51,233
Caught you!

219
00:13:51,367 --> 00:13:52,633
Hey, what is it, Mister?

220
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:54,200
Who are you?

221
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:56,267
It's me.
Why?

222
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:57,767
Why are you wearing that?

223
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:59,400
I didn't steal this, okay!

224
00:13:59,533 --> 00:14:01,967
And it belongs
to the woman earlier...

225
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,300
the one who bought from me.

226
00:14:03,433 --> 00:14:05,067
Where is she?
Tell me!

227
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,400
Show me!

228
00:14:06,533 --> 00:14:07,433
All right.

229
00:14:07,567 --> 00:14:09,033
Oh my god.

230
00:14:12,067 --> 00:14:13,467
That one.

231
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,700
There, he's looking
for the pretty lady.

232
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:19,100
Are you sure?

233
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:21,167
Yes, I'm sure.

234
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:22,667
That's him.

235
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,633
All right, thank you.

236
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:28,167
Be careful, okay?

237
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,500
Hey! What is that?

238
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,100
- She passed through here.
- Where?

239
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:02,233
Here, I promise.
It wasn't me, okay?

240
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,767
She passed through here.

241
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:07,267
That's her! She's the one
who bought from me!

242
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,333
There! That's her!

243
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:10,267
She's the one
who bought from me!

244
00:15:38,533 --> 00:15:39,933
Matias.

245
00:15:40,767 --> 00:15:42,367
What's going on here, Matias?

246
00:15:44,233 --> 00:15:46,100
So you do know each other?

247
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,333
How?

248
00:15:58,967 --> 00:16:00,433
I'll explain everything to you.

249
00:16:00,967 --> 00:16:02,533
Let's go to my office, Andrew.

250
00:16:25,267 --> 00:16:26,933
Hey, get in the car!

251
00:16:31,567 --> 00:16:33,100
Let's go!

252
00:16:43,767 --> 00:16:46,200
What do you need from
the woman you're chasing?

253
00:16:46,333 --> 00:16:47,667
Why should I tell you?

254
00:16:47,933 --> 00:16:48,800
Who are you anyway?

255
00:16:48,933 --> 00:16:50,167
Are you her father?

256
00:17:02,533 --> 00:17:03,833
Hey!

257
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,500
Hey, relax.

258
00:17:11,633 --> 00:17:13,367
They won't follow us.

259
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:15,067
You're safe now.

260
00:17:15,233 --> 00:17:16,767
Are you sure?

261
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,533
Of course, Joey.

262
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:20,733
How do you know my name?

263
00:17:20,867 --> 00:17:22,500
From your vlog.

264
00:17:22,633 --> 00:17:24,033
You know what?

265
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:27,067
I'm one of your twelve
followers.

266
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:29,367
Hey, look.

267
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:30,600
If you don't stop
the car right now,

268
00:17:30,733 --> 00:17:32,700
I'm going to jump out!

269
00:17:32,833 --> 00:17:35,133
Okay, go ahead.

270
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:38,433
But you'll be the one
who gets hurt, not me.

271
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,767
Okay, okay, okay, okay,
fine, fine.

272
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,300
Enough jokes.

273
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:46,700
I mean...

274
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,300
I just don't want you
to be afraid of me, okay?

275
00:17:51,833 --> 00:17:54,000
So, I'm Jin Ho,

276
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:55,333
and I will not hurt you.

277
00:17:55,467 --> 00:17:56,467
I promise.

278
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,600
I'll explain everything.

279
00:17:57,733 --> 00:17:59,167
Just...

280
00:17:59,767 --> 00:18:01,300
Trust me.

281
00:18:06,767 --> 00:18:10,133
<i>Mister, can you please
go faster?</i>

282
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,333
Matias is my business partner.

283
00:18:17,467 --> 00:18:20,500
We provide tracking services
for his textile business.

284
00:18:20,633 --> 00:18:22,167
Matias is just a bit antisocial,

285
00:18:22,333 --> 00:18:24,833
so I can't really invite him
to social gatherings.

286
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,267
Sorry about that, Mr. Dizon.

287
00:18:36,067 --> 00:18:38,267
I wasn't really going
to shoot you.

288
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,500
I was just trying to scare you
so you'd stop.

289
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:44,067
Just call me Andrew.

290
00:18:45,533 --> 00:18:48,633
And I'm sorry too
for suspecting you.

291
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,067
I'm just...

292
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,433
overprotective
when it comes to my family,

293
00:18:55,767 --> 00:18:59,200
especially after
what happened to my mom.

294
00:19:01,633 --> 00:19:02,667
I understand, Andrew,

295
00:19:03,833 --> 00:19:05,600
but you have nothing to fear

296
00:19:05,733 --> 00:19:07,767
now that you're under
my protection.

297
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,633
No one will hurt
any of you anymore.

298
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:24,300
You stop the car
and I'll trust you,

299
00:19:24,433 --> 00:19:25,867
then let's talk!

300
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:28,933
Then you'll run away.

301
00:19:30,067 --> 00:19:32,067
No, I won't! I promise!

302
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,300
I will listen to you.

303
00:19:33,433 --> 00:19:35,933
Besides, you saved me
from the bad guys.

304
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,333
You promise?

305
00:19:38,467 --> 00:19:39,867
I promise!

306
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,300
Okay, then...

307
00:19:56,533 --> 00:19:58,167
My name is Jin Ho.

308
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:00,100
Lee Jin Ho, and I'm from...

309
00:20:04,233 --> 00:20:05,233
You think I didn't know?

310
00:20:05,367 --> 00:20:06,667
You've been following me
since last night!

311
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,767
Ouch!

312
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:09,333
Stalker!

313
00:20:09,467 --> 00:20:12,333
Hey, hey, hey! Stop! Stop!

314
00:20:22,167 --> 00:20:24,600
<i> I have a gift for you.</i>

315
00:20:25,667 --> 00:20:27,767
<i>They say this is trendy.
You hang it on your bag.</i>

316
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:30,067
<i>- Isn't it cute?
- It's cute!</i>

317
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:37,633
Joey...

318
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:46,833
<i>- Dad.
- Joey!</i>

319
00:20:46,967 --> 00:20:48,400
<i>Where are you?
Are you safe?</i>

320
00:20:48,533 --> 00:20:49,500
I'm here at the market.

321
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:50,367
Where are you?

322
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,600
Someone chased me earlier.

323
00:20:52,733 --> 00:20:54,333
Good thing I managed to escape.

324
00:20:54,467 --> 00:20:56,433
And then my stalker saved me.

325
00:20:56,567 --> 00:20:57,633
What stalker?

326
00:20:57,767 --> 00:20:58,633
Dad, I'm okay.

327
00:20:58,767 --> 00:20:59,933
I can handle this.

328
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:03,367
<i> I'm here on San Isidro Street.</i>

329
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,667
Just meet me here

330
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,833
so we can face
this Korean guy alone.

331
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:26,500
Hey! Come back here!

332
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,800
The search warrant

333
00:21:38,933 --> 00:21:40,833
to ransack Major Delgado's
belongings has been issued.

334
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,167
Parak has already made a move

335
00:21:42,333 --> 00:21:43,467
to get Delgado jailed.

336
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:45,033
- Good job, Parak.
- This is the evidence

337
00:21:45,167 --> 00:21:46,633
that will clear your name.

338
00:21:46,767 --> 00:21:47,667
Where is it?

339
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:51,433
The gun he used to kill Orbos
is in his car.

340
00:21:51,567 --> 00:21:53,433
Sir, someone wants
to talk to you.

341
00:21:53,567 --> 00:21:55,933
Is it really true
that Major Delgado

342
00:21:56,067 --> 00:21:57,300
is the number one suspect?

343
00:21:57,433 --> 00:21:58,567
Mom, I need to go back
to the market.

344
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,333
I think I left
the flash drive there.

345
00:22:00,467 --> 00:22:03,133
Delgado has long been a thorn
in our side.

346
00:22:03,267 --> 00:22:04,767
It's good that he's finally
been silenced.

347
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:05,867
I want to tell this story

348
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:06,733
from a different angle.

349
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,133
Sir, I was set up!
